  <div class="box" id="what-is-edistrict">
    <h2>What is eDistrict UP?</h2>
    <p>eDistrict UP is the Uttar Pradesh government's online service-delivery platform for citizen certificates and related services. Through this single system, a resident of the state can apply for a certificate, follow its progress and download the final digitally signed document — without repeated trips to the tehsil or block office. The platform covers all 75 districts of Uttar Pradesh and brings together more than 325 services from 47 government departments.</p>
    <p>The system was launched in December 2008 under the National e-Governance Plan and is developed and run by the NIC UP State Unit, based at Yojana Bhawan in Lucknow. Since its launch, more than 36.90 crore certificates have been issued through it, which gives a sense of how central it has become to everyday paperwork in the state — scholarships, admissions, government jobs, bank work and court matters all routinely ask for certificates that originate here. In 2019, the platform received a Gems of Digital India Award (Analyst's Choice).</p>
    <p>One point that confuses many first-time users: citizens never deal with the "eDistrict" back office directly. Everything a citizen touches — registration, login, application, payment, status and download — happens on the citizen portal called <strong>eSathi</strong>, explained in the next section.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="info">
        <tr><th>Official portal</th><td>edistrict.up.gov.in</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Citizen login (eSathi)</th><td>esathi.up.gov.in</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Helpline</th><td>0522-2304706</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Email</th><td>ceghelpdesk@gmail.com</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Payment</th><td>PAYGOV — UPI, net banking, debit card</td></tr>
        <tr><th>DigiLocker</th><td>Connected — issued certificates are available at digilocker.gov.in</td></tr>
